# Q: is the rasputitsa a Σοβιετικοί advantage, and is the mud the weather ability's doing?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --mud-demo --probe tools/probe/mud.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/mud.txt
#
# Three tanks — Σοβιετικοί at slot 509, Δυτικοί at 508, Κινέζοι at 507 — at the near end of one lane
# each, twenty-eight metres apart, on ground this fixture has levelled to grass. All three are the
# same role with the same 400 mm-per-tick speed, so on this ground they are the same tank three
# times; what separates them is the school that designed the hull, and the ground is about to stop
# being grass.
#
# The mud is not a premise. The fixture clears the lane and gives team 0 the era, the design bureau
# and the materials that Έλεγχος Καιρού is behind; the `ability` line below is the Σοβιετικοί ability
# being called down through the world's own path, and the `attributes` pair either side of it is the
# ground changing because of it. If the strike were refused the lanes would still be grass and both
# columns would cover the same distance — which is what makes the difference below the weather's
# doing rather than the fixture's.
#
# Ground pressure has been a per-faction figure for a long time and mud has always been a surface
# with a movement cost; what was missing was that nothing on the *movement* path read that cost, so
# the pressure steered a route and did not set a speed. This is the same number, finally spent.

# --- the line-up, and the ground before the strike --------------------------------------------------
units
attributes -51 -257
attributes -51 -237

# --- the Σοβιετικοί call down the mud ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The strike lands on the second of those cells, at the ability's own 70 m radius and for its own
# 1 200 ticks, which covers the whole of all three lanes and then some. `attributes` on the same
# cell afterwards is the surface having changed, and the speed in every `unit` line below is that
# surface's doing.
ability WeatherControl -51 -237 0
tick 1
attributes -51 -237

# --- the orders -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Issued by the script, through the same command a click issues, and identical for the three: the
# same distance in a straight line up each of the three lanes. Nothing here favours anybody.
order 509 move -79 -182
order 508 move -51 -182
order 507 move -23 -182

# --- ten seconds of the same mud --------------------------------------------------------------------
# `unit` prints what each column covered and the ground line under it is the arithmetic: the surface
# under it, the pressure its school's hull puts on that surface, the cost those two make together,
# and the fraction of its nominal speed it is therefore left with.
tick 200
unit 509
unit 508
unit 507

# --- the ledger of measurements ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read off the three `travel` lines above and re-read the day the ground-pressure figures move.
#
# The Σοβιετικοί column covers about two thirds again what the Δυτικοί one does in the same ten
# seconds, on the same mud, at the same catalogue speed — heavy where it does not move, light where
# it does. The Κινέζοι hull presses hardest of the three and is last.
#
# These are not the whole of the arithmetic below them, and the difference is churn: a column wears
# the ground it drives over and a heavier one wears it faster, so the cost each pays rises as it
# goes — 216 ‰ for the Σοβιετικοί column and 281 ‰ for the Δυτικοί one against the 187 and 275 the
# same two would pay for being the first vehicle on a fresh cell. The gap widens with distance,
# which is the rasputitsa arriving rather than a bug in it.
expect "Σοβιετικοί metres of mud in ten seconds" 39 39 1
expect "Δυτικοί metres of mud in ten seconds" 23 23 1
expect "Κινέζοι metres of mud in ten seconds" 20 20 1
